### FundTrack API requests (VS Code REST Client)
### Click "Send Request" above each request to run it.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080

### 1. List clients → 200 OK
GET {{baseUrl}}/clients

### 1b. One client by id (Sarah) → 200 OK
GET {{baseUrl}}/clients/1

### 1c. Unknown client → 404 Not Found
GET {{baseUrl}}/clients/999

### 2. Create a valid client → 201 Created + Location header
POST {{baseUrl}}/clients
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Ali Khan",
  "subaccountNumber": "SA-100004"
}

### 3. Duplicate subaccount number (Sarah's) → 409 Conflict
POST {{baseUrl}}/clients
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Someone Else",
  "subaccountNumber": "SA-100001"
}

### 4. Blank name → 400 Bad Request (@NotBlank)
POST {{baseUrl}}/clients
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "   ",
  "subaccountNumber": "SA-100005"
}

### 5. Wrong subaccount format → 400 Bad Request (@Pattern)
POST {{baseUrl}}/clients
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Bad Format",
  "subaccountNumber": "ABC-1"
}

### 6. Missing field → 400 Bad Request (@NotBlank catches null)
POST {{baseUrl}}/clients
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "No Subaccount"
}

### 7. List funds → 200 OK (MPL100, NRT200, BND300)
GET {{baseUrl}}/funds

### 8. Create a NAV for NRT200 (fund 2) → 201 Created + Location
POST {{baseUrl}}/funds/2/nav
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "priceDate": "2026-11-03",
  "nav": 24.9800
}

### 9. Same fund, same date again → 409 Conflict (run after #8)
POST {{baseUrl}}/funds/2/nav
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "priceDate": "2026-11-03",
  "nav": 25.0000
}

### 10. Fund that doesn't exist → 404 Not Found
POST {{baseUrl}}/funds/999/nav
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "priceDate": "2026-11-03",
  "nav": 10.0000
}

### 11. Negative NAV → 400 Bad Request (@Positive)
POST {{baseUrl}}/funds/1/nav
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "priceDate": "2026-11-04",
  "nav": -5
}

### 12. Future date → 400 Bad Request (@PastOrPresent)
POST {{baseUrl}}/funds/1/nav
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "priceDate": "2099-01-01",
  "nav": 12.0000
}

### 13. Too many decimal places → 400 Bad Request (@Digits fraction = 4)
POST {{baseUrl}}/funds/1/nav
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "priceDate": "2026-11-04",
  "nav": 12.123456
}

### 14. NAV history for NRT200, newest first → 200 [ ... ]
GET {{baseUrl}}/funds/2/nav

### 15. NRT200's NAV on one date → 200 [ one item ] (the Location from #8)
GET {{baseUrl}}/funds/2/nav?date=2026-11-03

### 16. No NAV on that date → 200 [] (empty list, not 404)
GET {{baseUrl}}/funds/2/nav?date=2026-10-01

### 17. Unknown fund → 404
GET {{baseUrl}}/funds/999/nav

### 18. Invalid date in the query → 400 (Spring can't convert "banana" to a LocalDate)
GET {{baseUrl}}/funds/2/nav?date=banana
